    "created_at": "2016-07-01T08:39:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-01T08:39:29Z",
    "body": "The change looks fine editorially. How was this not needed for service workers?\n\nI also wonder a bit about the discussion in the other thread. It seems to me that worklets is the first platform instance of having multiple independent globals per realm. So maybe the module map is associated with realms, but the scripts run with a particular global.\n\nI basically wonder if we got the layering right or if we're working around a problem by just adding more hooks everywhere. It's starting to get increasingly more complicated how this works.\n",
